              supported: true,
              description: 'Multi-phase action: Phase 1—players ante and dealer deals 5 face-up; best poker hand wins pot. Phase 2—dealer calls ranks from the deck; players place a coin on each of their cards matching that rank; first with a coin on all five calls Bingo and wins all coins on the table. Phase 3 (Put and Take)—dealer turns 10 then 10 cards; players put then take coins by rank. Phase 4 (Count-Up)—dealer turns 13 cards counting ace to king; when rank matches position, everyone pays dealer that many coins.',
